"Play long-term games with long-term people." - Naval Ravikant

The best communities are built on trust and shared long-term vision.

The long-term vision for Vibe with AI is to be the most fun and approachable brand for the world to learn AI from.

Society needs to learn AI, but most people don't know it yet!

To get to know one another,r please introduce yourself below.

Copy/paste this template!
----

Hey, I'm {my name}.

I am {type of role}

I'm interested in learning {these topics/things/areas of AI}

Here are some things I've explored with AI:
{thing1}
{thing 2}
{thing 3}

\(If you haven't explored AI. That's cool, too!\)

Here is why I joined:
{short description}
----

True value creation happens when communities coalesce around service and vision.

Let's do it.

Cursor and Windsurf have AI Docs features...

But you have to keep them up to date manually

And they sometimes fail

enter Context7

a project that every doc you could want

Or you paste a GitHub repo, and it'll add them

The best part?

It uses MCPs, so you can call it as part of your global rules

How to add it to the cursor:

Go to: Settings -> Cursor Settings -> MCP -> Add new global MCP server

Pasting the following configuration into your Cursor ~/.cursor/mcp.json file is the recommended approach. See the Cursor MCP docs for more info.

{
"mcpServers": {
"context7": {
"command": "npx",
"args": \["-y", "@upstash/context7-mcp@latest"\]
}
}
}

Install in Windsurf
Add this to your Windsurf MCP config file. See Windsurf MCP docs for more info.

{
"mcpServers": {
"context7": {
"command": "npx",
"args": \["-y", "@upstash/context7-mcp@latest"\]
}
}
}

Install in VSCode
Add this to your VSCode MCP config file. See VSCode MCP docs for more info.

{
"servers": {
"Context7": {
"type": "stdio",
"command": "npx",
"args": \["-y", "@upstash/context7-mcp@latest"\]
}
}
}

